{{Quote|And of course, Therm Scissorpunch. No one's sure if he's ever actually done any of the terrible things he's always bragging about, but his name is Therm Scissorpunch, so who cares, right?|Savina Besatrix Malagán|<ref name="THRA221" />}}
'''Thermoculus Krisintvolt Scissorpunch''', also known simply as '''Therm Scissorpunch''' was a male [[Nephran]] from the [[planet]] [[Nepotis]] who lived in [[the galaxy]] for more than three [[Standard century|centuries]]. A [[gambler]] and [[pirate]], he became a [[Maz Kanata's pirate crew|close associate]] of the [[Pirate Queen|pirate queen]] [[Maz Kanata]] in the [[High Republic Era]] and defended her stake of the planet [[Takodana]] against the rival [[Dank Graks]] in a criminal [[Turf war with the Dank Graks|turf war]]. Scissorpunch lived through the [[Republic Era|fall of the Republic]] and the [[Imperial Era|rise of the Empire]]. His [[Gambling|card-playing]] habits saw him frequent the tables of the planet [[Vandor]], where he would play against the likes of scoundrels [[Landonis Balthazar Calrissian|Lando Calrissian]] and [[Han Solo]]. A particularly sore loser, he relied on his fearsome appearance to intimidate his opponents. The boastful Nephran had taken steps to enhance his fighting prowess with a sharpened shank implanted in his [[claw]], living up to the moniker that may or may not have been his true name.

==Biography==
===High Republic Era===
====Residence at Takodana Castle====
Thermoculus Krisintvolt Scissorpunch<ref name="THRA225" /> was born on the [[Nephran]] [[homeworld]] of [[Nepotis]].<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars NE" /> As an adult, many stories followed him, telling of terrible acts he had committed throughout [[the galaxy]]. Although the veracity of these tales was dubious, Scissorpunch entertained them nonetheless. During the [[High Republic Era]], he frequented the [[Takodana Castle|castle]] of [[Pirate Queen|pirate queen]] [[Maz Kanata]], an establishment on the planet [[Takodana]] where all manner of criminals and [[pirate]]s were welcome. During one evening at Kanata's<ref name="THRA221" /> in [[382 BBY]],<ref name="THRA Date">''[[Star Wars: The High Republic Character Encyclopedia]]'' dates the events of [[The High Republic Adventures (2022) 1|''The High Republic Adventures'' (2022) 1]] to [[382 BBY]].</ref> Scissorpunch was playing a [[Gambling|game of cards]] when a brawl broke out between former lovers [[Alak]] and [[Raf Thatchburn]], the latter a member of the [[Galactic Antipiracy Command]]. Scissorpunch and fellow pirate [[Coromont Vizzle]] leapt to Alak's side, but the fight was soon broken up by Kanata, who ejected Thatchburn from the castle. That same night, [[prospector]] [[Dexter Jettster]] and undercover-[[Padawan|Jedi Padawan]] [[Savina Besatrix Malagán|Sav Malagán]] informed [[Maz Kanata's pirate crew|Kanata's crew]] that the rival [[Dank Graks]] were preparing for an all-out [[Turf war with the Dank Graks|turf war]] for Takodana.<ref name="THRA221" />

====Fighting the Dank Graks====
Scissorpunch travelled with the crew on Kanata's [[starship]], the ''[[Venomed Scabbard]]'', to investigate the Graks' seemingly-abandoned ship above the planet and discover more about their plans. On the ''[[Grim Devourer]]'', the Nephran searched the lower levels with the [[cyborg]] [[Quiet Shan]] until being interrupted by blasts from the ''Scabbard'', commandeered by the Graks and their leader, the [[Geonosian]] [[Arkik Von]]. Since the [[Sorcerers of Tund|Tund technology]] that powered the ''Devourer'' was operable only by those [[Force-sensitive|sensitive]] to [[the Force]], Scissorpunch and the rest of the crew relied on Kanata's piloting until the [[Skirmish above Takodana|firefight]] was interrupted by [[Inspector]] Thatchburn. The pirate queen escaped via [[hyperspace]] and instructed her crew to rest before their next step: seeking out Von's frequent haunts for more information.<ref name="THRA222">[[The High Republic Adventures (2022) 2|''The High Republic Adventures'' (2022) 2]]</ref>

After some time, the crew received word from [[Abadoo]], Kanata’s [[pilot]] for the ''Venomed Scabbard'' who, as a [[Hoover]], had been able to stay out of sight of the Graks. Abadoo informed them that Von was leading the Graks to [[Frander's hidden depot|Frander’s hidden depot]] and they quickly followed. When they arrived, Kanata remained on the ''Devourer'', while the rest of the crew ventured out to find the Graks attempting to intimidate [[Frander]] into handing over his [[Spiral-class Viz-Core Eviscerator|''Spiral''-class Viz-Core Eviscerators]]. However, Von had set a trap; he had detected Abadoo through the Force when aboard the ''Scabbard'' and, once Kanata had landed, had sent the towering [[Muun]] [[Drrn]] to sneak aboard the ''Devourer'' and capture Kanata. The Graks beat a hasty retreat, commandeering one of the Eviscerators and spraying Scissorpunch and his comrades with fire, forcing them to take cover. They could then only watch as the ''Devourer'' lifted off from the depot with Kanata captive aboard. Returning to reclaim the ''Scabbard'', the group also realized that Malagán was missing.<ref name="THRA223">[[The High Republic Adventures (2022) 3|''The High Republic Adventures'' (2022) 3]]</ref> The Padawan had taken her own Eviscerator to follow the Graks and was able to gain access to the group, posing as a Force user affiliated with the [[Graf family]]. She was able to contact the ''Scabbard'' and inform the group that the Graks were headed to [[Jedha]]. As the ''Scabbard'' came out of hyperspace above the moon, Scissorpunch argued with Alak about the latter’s decision to request backup from Thatchburn, however it soon became apparent that they would need it – they had arrived in the midst of a [[Battle of Jedha|battle]].<ref name="THRA224">[[The High Republic Adventures (2022) 4|''The High Republic Adventures'' (2022) 4]]</ref>

====The Battle of Jedha====
The battle involved various different parties – the militaries of the planets [[Eiram]] and [[E'ronoh|E’ronoh]], local rioters, [[Jedi]], the [[Guardians of the Whills]], and the Force cult known as the [[Path of the Open Hand]].<ref name="The High Republic: The Battle of Jedha">''[[The High Republic: The Battle of Jedha]]''</ref> Fighting their way through this fracas, Scissorpunch and his comrades attempted to find Malagán and Kanata. Scissorpunch was particularly overwhelmed by the conflict, causing Vizzle to question why he was nervous, given his notorious reputation as a pirate. Scissorpunch admitted that many of the stories told about him were in fact made up. He then received a pep-talk from Vizzle’s court-assigned officer, [[Rado]], who rode around in Vizzle’s backpack. Rado made Scissorpunch realize that he was his own biggest detractor. As the group attempted to make it to the tapbar [[Enlightenment]] they were confronted by a huge group of rioters. Scissorpunch, riled up by Rado, charged ahead into the group, barrelling into the rioters and successfully driving them away.<ref name="THRA225">[[The High Republic Adventures (2022) 5|''The High Republic Adventures'' (2022) 5]]</ref> Shortly afterwards, they came across the Path of the Open Hand, with the young [[Gran]] [[Tromak]] presenting Scissorpunch with a flower as an offering. Scissorpunch responded by chopping the flower in half, causing Tromak to burst into tears and for the Path Elder [[Barbatash]] to attack the group. They managed to drive Barbatash off, but Scissorpunch went into a battle frenzy and joined in with the rioters trashing the streets. He was only brought to his senses by the arrival of the [[Jedi Master]] [[Silandra Sho]], whose appearance caused him to flee the scene back to his friends, who decided to regroup at the ''Scabbard''.<ref name="THRA226">[[The High Republic Adventures (2022) 6|''The High Republic Adventures'' (2022) 6]]</ref>

====Rescuing Kanata on Takodana====
Once back aboard Kanata’s ship, they were finally rejoined by Malagán, who had been on an adventure of her own. The Padawan informed them that Kanata had been taken back to Takodana by Von, at which point Von himself contacted the crew to gloat over the fact that he had taken over [[Takodana Castle]] with an army of enforcer droids provided by the Grafs. The group resolved to attempt a rescue anyway, but as they approached the castle the ''Scabbard'' was shot down by guided missiles fired by Von’s forces. They were then attacked in the forest by his enforcer droids but were ultimately led to safety by one of Kanata’s associates, [[Bumblehead Bim]], who took them to his hideout. The crew believed the situation to be futile, but Malagán nevertheless snuck off to attempt to rescue Kanata by herself.<ref name="THRA227">[[The High Republic Adventures (2022) 7|''The High Republic Adventures'' (2022) 7]]</ref> Though initially imprisoned, Malagán managed to send Inspector Thatchburn – who had also been captured – to tell the crew to draw Von’s enforcer droids away from the castle. Scissorpunch and his comrades did just that, engaging the droids on the shores of [[Nymeve Lake|Lake Nymeve]]. As the battle raged, they were joined by a contingent of Jedi sent from the [[Jedi Temple (Takodana)|nearby temple]] and together they helped storm the castle, capture Von, and free Kanata. That night, with the castle's usual crowd back in residence, Scissorpunch joined his friends to celebrate the return to normality and the heroic efforts of Padawan Malagán.<ref name="THRA228">[[The High Republic Adventures (2022) 8|''The High Republic Adventures'' (2022) 8]]</ref>

===Age of the Empire===
During the time of the [[Imperial Era]], Scissorpunch considered himself an "independent entrepreneur," though he still enjoyed a good card game and became a regular at [[Fort Ypso]] on the planet [[Vandor]].<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars NE" /> In [[10 BBY]],<ref name="TOG" /> he played a game of [[sabacc]] at the seedy establishment against a host of beings that included the famed [[smuggler]] [[Landonis Balthazar Calrissian|Lando Calrissian]].<ref name="Solo" /> That particular game saw Scissorpunch lose to Calrissian, a situation so upsetting that the Nephran briefly considered snapping the man's neck, though he ultimately decided against this.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars NE" /> Scissorpunch continued to play at the table as newcomer [[Han Solo]] joined, an up-and-coming smuggler who also lost to Calrissian.<ref name="Solo" />

Sometime after the [[Battle of Yavin]], Scissorpunch came into contact with the [[mercenary]] [[Saponza]] and [[Saponza's partner|his partner]] and entreated them to acquire [[coaxium]] for his [[boss]].<ref name="Commander">''[[Star Wars: Commander]]'' "Lucky Break, Part I" Version 6.1.0</ref> An [[Unidentified artist|artist]] who traveled the galaxy cataloging various species and individuals included a short entry on the Nephran in his [[Unidentified artist's journal|journal]], where he noted that "Threm Scissorpunch" was likely a name the gambler had given himself.<ref name="Alien Archive" />

==Personality and traits==
Therm Scissorpunch was a braggart who consistently spoke of the many fearsome acts he had undertaken.<ref name="THRA221" /> His imposing features paired well with this behavior; he relied on intimidation as a mechanism against critique.<ref name="Alien Archive" /> Scissorpunch's temper was short, increasingly aggravated in the event that he lost money while gambling. This sore-loser mentality gave way to passing thoughts of violence against his opponents, in some cases even considering murder. Whatever feelings boiled inside his shell, however, Scissorpunch hid his emotions behind his thick exoskeleton.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars NE" /> And despite his pugnacious attitude, he remained loyal to those he trusted, leaping to their side should they need help.<ref name="THRA221" />

==Skills and abilities==
Contrary to his boasts, Scissorpunch was a mostly mediocre gambler. He relied more on his intimidating phyique than his skill with cards to win games.<ref name="DB">{{Databank|therm-scissorpunch|Therm Scissorpunch}}</ref>

==Equipment==
Scissorpunch's claw was equipped with a shank implanted into his shell that augmented his combat performance.<ref name="Alien Archive" />

==Behind the scenes==
Therm Scissorpunch<ref name="Topps">{{Topps|set=2018 Topps Denny's Solo: A Star Wars Story|cardname=Therm Scissorpunch}}</ref> was first revealed in a [[Wikipedia:Denny's|Denny's]] commercial for the ''[[Star Wars Anthology Series]]'' film ''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]'', released on [[April 2]], [[2018]].<ref name="Denny's">{{OfficialYouTube|channel=@dennys|name=Denny's|video=s8q-y2NkIK0|text=Solo: A Star Wars Story exclusive trading cards, available only at Denny's!|date=2018-04-02|nolive=1}}</ref> Scissorpunch was later identified by name in a Denny's-exclusive [[Topps]] trading card for ''Solo''.<ref name="Topps" />

